@startuml timeline-query
title US-14: Timeline Query - Position Track and Proximity Events Reconstructed

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

actor Operator
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
participant "Express API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nposition_history" as TSDB
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j

Operator -> Dashboard : opens alert for VesselB
Dashboard -> API : GET /alerts/:alert_id/investigation

API -> TSDB : SELECT observed_at, lat, lon, geo_cell\nFROM position_history\nWHERE entity_id = 'VesselB'\nAND observed_at BETWEEN $window_start AND $window_end\nORDER BY observed_at ASC

note over TSDB
  Hypertable partitioned by observed_at (ADR-002, ADR-006).
  TimescaleDB chunk exclusion eliminates all chunks
  outside the requested time window.
  geo_cell is an indexed column — not a partition dimension.
  Query hits only the relevant time chunks.
  Not a full table scan.
end note

TSDB --> API : position track [ { timestamp_ms, lat, lon }, ... ]

API -> Neo4j : MATCH (b:Entity {id: 'VesselB'})-[e:PROXIMITY_EVENT]-(other)\nWHERE e.episode_start_ms BETWEEN $window_start AND $window_end\nRETURN other.id, e.episode_start_ms, e.last_seen_ms,\n  e.lat, e.lon, e.distance_at_detection, e.min_distance_metres,\n  exists((b)-[:KNOWN_ASSOCIATE]-(other)) AS known

note over Neo4j
  Single Cypher traversal from VesselB node.
  Each PROXIMITY_EVENT edge represents one episode
  (not one ping). episode_start_ms is the idempotency
  key component and episode anchor.
  Returns all proximity episodes in the window
  with a flag indicating whether the other
  entity was a known associate.
end note

Neo4j --> API : proximity episodes\n[ { entity_id, episode_start_ms, last_seen_ms,\n  distance_at_detection, min_distance_metres, known }, ... ]

API --> Dashboard : investigation response\n{ position_track, proximity_events }
Dashboard --> Operator : entity track rendered on map\nproximity events overlaid as markers on timeline

@enduml
